+// A profile directory does not namespace OSCrypt's macOS keychain item, and a
+// keychain item's ACL trusts the signatures that created it. Every Crest bundle
+// therefore takes a Crest-owned item of its own, keyed on its bundle ID:
+// sharing Chromium's item is what makes macOS ask for the login password when a
+// differently signed Crest build opens it. A Crest bundle never falls through
+// to the shared Chromium name. Normal Chromium builds keep their upstream ones.
+//
+// These names are frozen. OSCrypt's key is derived from this keychain item, and
+// every profile's tracked-preference validators — `protection.macs.*_encrypted_hash`
+// and `protection.super_encrypted_hash` in `Secure Preferences` — are encrypted
+// with it. Renaming an item rotates the key, every encrypted validator then
+// fails to decrypt, and `PrefHashStoreImpl` treats a stale encrypted hash as
+// CHANGED_ENCRYPTED without ever consulting the legacy HMAC beside it: the
+// enforced tracked preferences are reset on first launch. `extensions.settings`
+// is one of them, so a rename silently uninstalls every extension in every
+// Space while leaving the pinned tiles behind. This happened once, in 0.6.96.
+//
+// Adoption retires the encrypted validators of the profiles it moves, which
+// makes that one migration safe, but nothing repairs a rename outside adoption.
+// Add a new bundle ID rather than renaming a shipped one.
+std::string CrestKeychainName(bool service) {
+  const std::string bundle(base::apple::BaseBundleID());
+  constexpr std::string_view kCrest = "com.pauldavis.crest";
+  if (bundle != kCrest && !bundle.starts_with("com.pauldavis.crest.")) {
+    return service ? kDefaultServiceName : kDefaultAccountName;
+  }
+  if (!service) {
+    return bundle;
+  }
+  if (bundle == kCrest) {
+    return "Crest Safe Storage";
+  }
+  const std::string suffix = bundle.substr(kCrest.size() + 1);
+  if (suffix == "control-plane.chromium") {
+    return "Crest Review Safe Storage";
+  }
+  if (suffix == "chromium-baseline") {
+    return "Crest Chromium Baseline Safe Storage";
+  }
+  return "Crest " + suffix + " Safe Storage";
+}
